Dragon tile) has minimal synergy with my current hand structure, which is leaning toward suited tile combinations. Keeping the J1 pair only provides 2 points (Dragon Pung) if completed, while maintaining my B4-B5-B6 sequence and T1-T2 combinations offers better paths to higher-scoring patterns like Half Flush or Pure Shifted Chows. With only 3 J1 tiles unshown and no clear path to a dragon-based high-scoring pattern, J1 is the safest discard.\n\nAnswer: Play J1"}
