e depleted tile pool and weak hand structure, forcing a Chi here doesn't improve my winning chances significantly.\n\nReason: \nPassing is the better choice because: (1) My hand lacks a clear winning structure even after Chi; (2) Exposing melds early with such a weak hand reduces scoring potential; (3) The tile pool is heavily depleted, making it difficult to complete a winning hand quickly; (4) Maintaining flexibility is more valuable than forcing an early meld that doesn't significantly advance my position.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
